From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: AVFoundation bindings for both sinks

Replaces upstream's driver with the Objective-C side of the rebuilt
output, which makes every Apple framework call for the C modules of
patches 0012 to 0015:

- ao_avfoundation.m: driver registration with the ao-avfoundation-*
  options (max-lookahead exists on tvOS only), the output's serial queue,
  tagged so that work already on it runs inline, the AVAudioSession calls
  behind TARGET_OS_IPHONE, mpv's logging, reads and reload requests for
  the C side, and the routing of every driver call to the sink init
  opened;
- ao_avfoundation_av.h: the state the Objective-C files share;
- ao_avfoundation_pcm_av.m: AVSampleBufferAudioRenderer and
  AVSampleBufferRenderSynchronizer, sample buffer creation, the restart
  observers and the bounded tvOS feed timer; the renderer set-up and
  buffer handling follow upstream's file;
- ao_avfoundation_compressed_av.m: AVPlayer (no automatic stall waiting,
  no external playback), one fixed asset address per format, a new asset
  and item (plain initialiser) for every start after a reset, the
  resource loader (content type, a 2 GiB content length, no byte ranges),
  which serves only the current asset's requests, the 50 ms feed timer,
  volume and mute on the player, and compressed-buffer as the device
  buffer.

The C side's renderer-failed and item-ready values are checked against
AVFoundation's at compile time. The macOS device list and device selection
stay as patch 0002 left them, and "please use coreaudio_exclusive instead"
is still logged only where the CoreAudio output exists.

